ication-symbol scheme="EC">B21B  38/00V</classification-symbol></classification-ecla><invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="EN">METHOD AND APPARATUS FOR DETECTING CHATTERING OF COLD ROLLING MILL</invention-title><invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="FR">PROCEDE ET DISPOSITIF PERMETTANT DE DECELER LE BROUTAGE D'UN LAMINOIR A FROID</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-52002708-B"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>52002708</doc-number><kind>B</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-60137512-A" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>60137512</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6035004-B" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6035004</doc-number><kind>B</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8108205-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8108205</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1125649A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWASAKI STEEL CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KODAMA TOSHIFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TORAO AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWASAKI STEEL CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KODAMA, TOSHIFUMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORAO, AKIRA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KODAMA TOSHIFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TORAO AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KODAMA, TOSHIFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORAO, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The invention provides a method of quickly and accurately detecting the chattering of a rolling mill during cold rolling. The presence of chattering is determined using a plurality of acoustic parameters derived from sounds measured near a rolling mill during cold rolling. The acoustic parameters include the sound intensities of the frequency band characteristic of the chattering and the Nth overtone frequency band, the peak frequency of the sound frequency component distribution, the resonance coefficient, and the peak intensity. The same parameter may be measured at different instants, processed and used as different parameters.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé permettant de déceler rapidement et précisément le broutage d'un laminoir à froid en cours de fonctionnement. On décèle le broutage sur la base de plusieurs paramètres acoustiques fournis par des mesures sonores effectuées près de l'installation en cours de fonctionnement. Ces paramètres sont les suivants: intensités sonores de la bande de fréquence caractéristique du broutage et de la bande de fréquence d'harmonique supérieur (nième), fréquence de crête de la distribution des composantes de fréquence sonore, coefficient de résonance et intensité de crête. Il est possible de mesurer les mêmes paramètres à des instants différents, puis de les traiter et de les utiliser en tant que paramètres différents.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>